Fixtures for a range in the next valid tokens. The grammar expects a
range after "x", so the failure records `"a".."c"`, kind range. Each
.next_tokens member is the output of `ohm-cli test next_tokens`, which
tests a range with its first character. These fixtures compile the
grammar with docker. See error-reporting prd section 10.9.
-- grammar.ohm --
Range {
  S = "x" "a".."c" end
}
-- bad.txt --
xq
-- bad.N.expected --
range "a".."c"
-- bad.N.next_tokens --
range "a".."c": match succeeded
-- short.txt --
x
-- short.N.expected --
range "a".."c"
-- short.N.next_tokens --
range "a".."c": match succeeded
